From 3dc9b05924b9875ebfb2a39194d5c00bf77ff3e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:41:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arrange: pruning-at-scale experiments (-DPRETEST,
 -DSURV_FIX, -DPRUNE_DIAG)

Scratch experiments for the large-N cost study (cx/prune), all compiled
out by default (the default build visits the same nodes as fdb77fc:
quick 1,770,779, full 14,958,507, prod 50,375,738).

- PRETEST: the children five or more vectors deep (nearly all (2,3)/(3,2))
  first run the count and forward checks that follow their two filters on
  counts and unions only (FILTER_COUNT: no compress, no store); the ones
  that die there are exactly the ones the real filters would kill, so the
  nodes and squares are unchanged. Env PRETEST_MIN (default 5).
- SURV_FIX: the (2,2) children that survive the cascade get cross support
  and the support filter iterated to their fixpoint (env SURV_FIX_MIN,
  SURV_FIX_ROUNDS; FORCE_AFTER forces the cascade order).
- PRUNE_DIAG: reference implementations of cross, cell (exactly-once) and
  pair support iterated to their fixpoints, evaluated on copies of the
  lists of sampled (2,2) children, searched (2,2) and (1,2)/(2,1) nodes,
  with the MRV count before/after; a timed build of the exactly-once
  relation at the (1,1) nodes; the possible diagonals at (1,2)/(2,1)
  nodes (PD_DIAG_ONLY). JSON to env PD_OUT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
